Change: Honour the sub-admin switch when listing group administrators

With `allow_subadmins` turned off, sub-admins could no longer act, but
the group listings still reported who held the role: getSubAdminsGroups(),
getGroupsSubAdmins() and getAllSubAdmins() answered from the database regardless
of the setting. Administration pages built on them showed a group as "managed by"
people who had no such permission any more.

The three read paths now follow the same switch as the permission checks. A real
administrator keeps the full listing, so the existing behaviour of treating
administrators as sub-admins of every group is unaffected.
